        "raw": "<p>Today my wife and I taught a friend Sentinels. We played with Unity, The Argent Adept, Tempest and Ra. Being out first game we played again Baron Blade in normal mode in the Insula Primalis. There was a lot of synergy and we ended up having the volcano make the crushing blow on Baron Blade (achievement unlocked) :) ... But then our friend said... lets keep playing. We went to reset the game when he said, &quot;No let just bring another villian out and leave the rest the same.&quot; So... we brought out Omnitron (again on normal mode) and ended up defeating her(he?, it?) as well. I was wondering if anyone had done a &quot;campaign mode&quot; of sorts with villians like this before, at least with the less difficult villians it was lots of fun, and still a challenge as we had spent a lot of health and resources to defeat the first villian. He also enjoyed being able to keep on going without having to learn another character or get a new set up in order to keep on playing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thoughts? Other experiences new players have brough to the table which has enriched the game for you?</p>",
