      {
        "id": 38577,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-14T21:25:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There's a thread somewhere on the forums about someone who tried to do exactly what you're talking about - stringing together fights where the heroes get a slight rest between fights, maybe heal a bit, but you have to keep going with whoever survived the last fight.&nbsp; I think the consensus was that it was a fun idea but still needed some tweaking because for every fight after the first, the heroes will not have to go through their normal build-up phase of getting cards into play and so are extraordinarily powerful from the first instant the new villain walks onto the stage.&nbsp; Tachnyon specifically can be extra powerful in later fights since her trash will be full of Burst cards.</p><p>I also dabbled in something similar to his.&nbsp; I've got a series of scenarios that link together individual fights to tell a story like a comic book arc.&nbsp; It's different, though, in that each fight is a regular fight.&nbsp; You can find my scenarios on my website: www.spiffworld.com/sotm.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:20.241Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
